.TH ROUE 1 "2026" "roue 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
roue \- drag-and-drop file converter for the Linux desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B roue
.RI [ PRESET ] " FILE" ...
.br
.B roue
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B roue
converts files with presets: HEIC to JPG, MOV to MP4, video to GIF, Word to
PDF, "under 10 MB" for chat apps, and more. Results are written next to the
originals and never overwrite an existing file. Everything runs locally with
FFmpeg, libvips (or ImageMagick), Ghostscript, Pandoc and LibreOffice.
.PP
Without arguments in a desktop session,
.B roue
opens the full panel. The everyday way in is the wheel: a radial menu of the
presets that fit your files, opened by Ctrl+Shift+right-click on files in
Files, by "Convert with Roue..." in the Files right-click menu, by the hotkey
(Super+Shift+D, Super being the Windows key, which runs
.BR "roue wheel" ),
or by holding Shift while dragging a file on X11.
.PP
.B roue PRESET FILE...
is a shorthand for
.BR "roue convert PRESET FILE..." .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "convert " "PRESET FILE..."
Convert files or folders with a preset.
.RS
.TP
.BI "\-o, \-\-output\-dir " DIR
Write results to DIR instead of next to the originals.
.TP
.BI "\-j, \-\-jobs " N
Number of parallel conversions (default: one per CPU core).
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-recursive
Include files in sub-folders of dropped folders.
.TP
.B \-\-notify
Show a desktop notification when done.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print results as JSON.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Only print errors.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Show the tool's output when a conversion fails.
.RE
.TP
.BR "list " [ \-\-for " FILE...] [" \-\-group " GROUP] [" \-\-all "] [" \-\-json ]
List presets, optionally only those that fit the given files.
.TP
.BI "info " FILE...
Show the detected type, media details and matching presets.
.TP
.B doctor
Check which conversion tools and desktop integrations are installed.
.TP
.BR "history " [ \-n " N]"
Show recent conversions.
.TP
.B undo
Move the results of the last conversion to the trash.
.TP
.BR "setup " [ \-\-binding " KEYS] [" \-\-no\-hotkey "] [" \-\-no\-nautilus "] [" \-\-restart\-files "] [" \-\-remove ]
Add the app launcher, the D-Bus service, the Files right-click menu and the
hotkey (GNOME) for the current user. The hotkey runs
.BR "roue wheel" .
Parts already installed by a system package are skipped.
.TP
.BR "wheel " [FILE...]
Open the wheel. With files, or without files while files are selected in
Files (in front), the wheel at the pointer, showing the presets that fit them.
Otherwise an empty ring to drop files on (click it to choose files; it also
uses files copied with Ctrl+C). Its last slice, More..., opens the full panel.
.TP
.BR "panel " [ \-\-preferences "] [FILE...]"
Open the full panel, optionally with files ready to convert.
.TP
.B quit
Stop Roue running in the background.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if a conversion failed, 2 on usage errors (such as an unknown
preset), 130 when interrupted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/roue/settings.yaml
Settings shared by the wheel, the panel, the CLI and the Files menu.
.TP
.I ~/.config/roue/presets/*.yaml
Your own presets. A preset with the same id as a built-in one replaces it.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/roue/history.jsonl
The last 50 conversions, used by
.B history
and
.BR undo .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colours in terminal output.
.TP
.B ROUE_DISABLE_TOOLS
Comma-separated tool ids to treat as missing (for testing fallbacks).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR vips (1),
.BR gs (1),
.BR pandoc (1)
.PP
Documentation: https://guilyx.github.io/roue/docs/
